## Initial Access Prerequisites

Submit these baseline entitlement requests via the corporate self-service portal so credentials provision in the background while you review the guides:

| Platform System | Entitlement Group | Required Purpose | Validation Command |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Enterprise GitHub** | `org-mobile-engineering` | Clone core repositories and templates | `ssh -T git@git.enterprise.internal` |
| **Artifact Registry** | `pkg-mobile-artifacts-read` | Pull shared Maven, CocoaPods &amp; npm packages | `curl -I https://registry.enterprise.internal/health` |
| **Bitrise CI / CD** | `bitrise-mobile-engineers` | Trigger builds and inspect PR status | Bitrise dashboard console login |
| **Figma Design System** | `design-mobile-tokens` | Access unified UI components and design specs | Figma workspace project access |

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">FOUNDATIONAL PLATFORM GUARDRAILS</div>
  <p>Keep these non-negotiable principles in mind as you progress through each track:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Strict Layered Separation:</strong> UI components must only observe ViewModel state; direct repository or network calls from view layers are strictly prohibited.</li>
    <li><strong>Zero Plaintext Credentials:</strong> API secrets, auth tokens, and certificates must always reside in secure storage (KeyStore / Keychain), never in source control.</li>
    <li><strong>Offline-First Resilience:</strong> All features touching network endpoints must implement caching and Circuit Breaker resilience.</li>
    <li><strong>Automated Gate Compliance:</strong> Every pull request must pass Danger PR Bot static analysis and unit test suites prior to merge.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
